  "reveal": {
    "brief_voiced": "The killer was Aziz. The touch faltered twice. Fides tripped about the third minute of the touch; the green hand's own trip — a new hand's stumble convicts nobody, and the tower thinks no worse of it. But Spes hung late where the method wanted her elsewhere, and no custom excuses it; that rope was in Aziz's keeping, and the hands that should have held it were free about the first minute of the touch. Lady Lavinia Loveless did not survive the office.\n\nAs to the why of it: Of Aziz, the playbill says: Aziz — Xerxes's companion, constant at his side; a fixture no one enquires into. Of Lady Lavinia Loveless: Lady Lavinia Loveless — a faded actress turned medium; apt to let people rather too close.\n\nThe tower proved every pair of hands but one.",
